# Operator e2e credential tokens for `pnpm test:e2e` / `pnpm test:e2e:batch`.
#
# Copy this file to tests/.env.e2e and fill in the values you need. The e2e
# runner loads it at startup (see tests/e2e/utils/e2e-env-file.ts) — REAL ENV
# WINS: any value already exported in your shell or set by CI is left
# untouched, this file only fills gaps. tests/.env.e2e itself is gitignored;
# only this value-free .example is committed. CI never uses this file — it
# sets these same variables via GitHub Environments.
#
# Values here never leave this machine: they populate process.env for this
# CLI process and its spawned children (ssh/pulumi/docker) only — never
# written to a deployed server or client bundle (see the 'operator-secret'
# class in src/lib/config-registry.js).
#
# Object-storage credentials follow one convention across every provider:
#   <PROVIDER>_ACCESS_KEY / <PROVIDER>_SECRET_KEY / <PROVIDER>_STORAGE_REGION
# keyed off the same <PROVIDER> prefix as <PROVIDER>_API_TOKEN. This file is
# kept in exact operator-secret parity with src/lib/config-registry.js
# (pinned by tests/unit/lib/credential-key-convention.test.ts).
#
# Selection → credential map (scenario tokens are `provider/mode`, e.g.
# `hetzner/compose`; a run's required credentials are registry-driven —
# tests/config.ts `e2e.providers[provider].requiredEnv`):
#   --provider hetzner (default; release-gating) → Hetzner block
#   --provider digitalocean                      → DigitalOcean block
#   --provider linode                            → Linode block
#   --provider vultr                             → Vultr block
#   --provider scaleway                          → Scaleway block + Cloudflare
#
# Every leg uses its OWN provider's DNS, so it needs only its own block. The
# one exception is scaleway/*: no scaleway-dns.js backend exists yet, so s1
# stays on Cloudflare DNS.
#
# DNS is a DEFAULT, not a fixture: any backend with a base domain can be asked
# for on any scenario via the refinement (`hetzner/k8s-ha-cloudflare`,
# `digitalocean/compose-cloudflare`). Add that backend's token below when you
# do. Setting E2E_DNS_PROVIDER instead moves EVERY scenario at once.

# ─── Vibecarbon license ── required by BOTH integration and e2e ──────────────
# A real Ed25519-signed Fullerene key. Paid deploy modes (compose-ha, k8s,
# k8s-ha) gate on one, and there is no dev bypass: VIBECARBON_DEV_LICENSE used
# to skip signature verification, but it shipped inside the npm package, so it
# was also a free Fullerene grant to any customer who read validator.js.
#
# Mint one (needs the signing key, which only the maintainer holds):
#   VIBECARBON_LICENSE_PRIVATE_KEY=... node scripts/generate-license.js --email you@example.com
#
# The integration harness reads this variable directly (it builds its own fake
# HOME). The e2e harness does NOT — its CLI children read ~/.vibecarbon/license,
# so activate it once as a customer would:
#   node src/cli.js activate "$VIBECARBON_TEST_LICENSE_KEY"
VIBECARBON_TEST_LICENSE_KEY=''

# ─── Hetzner Cloud ── release-gating matrix (hetzner/*) ──────────────────────
# Required for every release-gating scenario. The API token also drives
# Hetzner DNS-01 for hetzner/compose, hetzner/compose-ha and hetzner/k8s
# (e1/e2/e3) — one token covers Cloud and DNS, and the separate DNS Console
# was retired in May 2026.
HETZNER_API_TOKEN=''

# Hetzner Object Storage (S3-compatible) keys — backup/restore steps use S3
# as the wal-g target. Required for every release scenario.
HETZNER_ACCESS_KEY=''
HETZNER_SECRET_KEY=''

# ─── Cloudflare DNS ── scaleway/* only, plus any `-cloudflare` override ──────
# Every leg now defaults to its own provider's DNS, so this token is needed
# only for scaleway/compose (s1), which has no DNS backend yet. It is also
# required if you explicitly ask any scenario for Cloudflare via the DNS
# refinement, e.g. `hetzner/k8s-ha-cloudflare` — every backend with a base
# domain is selectable on every scenario.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=''

# ─── DigitalOcean ── opt-in (`--provider digitalocean`, digitalocean/*) ──────
# Not needed for the release-gating matrix. Personal access token (Full Access).
# One token covers both compute and DNS-01 for d1/d2/d3 — DigitalOcean's
# solver ships in cert-manager core, so the k8s leg needs no webhook chart.
DIGITALOCEAN_API_TOKEN=''

# Spaces (S3-compatible) keys — created in the DO console (Spaces →
# Access Keys), separate credentials from the API token.
DIGITALOCEAN_ACCESS_KEY=''
DIGITALOCEAN_SECRET_KEY=''

# OPTIONAL — standing DO project id for ensureProjectAssignment (env-first):
# when set, e2e deploys file droplets into this project instead of
# find-or-creating one per run. Point it at the dedicated e2e project.
DIGITALOCEAN_PROJECT_ID=''

# ─── Linode (Akamai) ── opt-in (`--provider linode`, linode/compose) ─────────
# Not needed for the release-gating matrix. Personal access token, 64 alphanumeric
# chars (cloud.linode.com → Profile → API Tokens, Select All Read/Write).
# Also drives Linode DNS-01 for l1. NOTE: Linode serves a zone from its
# nameservers only while the account holds at least one active Linode, so
# between runs `linode.appcarbon.dev` answers REFUSED and the zone publishes
# again once the run's instance exists. That is expected, not a broken token.
LINODE_API_TOKEN=''

# Object Storage (S3-compatible) keys — created in the Linode console
# (Object Storage → Access Keys), separate credentials from the API token.
# NOTE: creating the first key activates Object Storage on the account
# (flat monthly base fee, ~$5/mo).
LINODE_ACCESS_KEY=''
LINODE_SECRET_KEY=''
# Linode assigns each ACCOUNT one storage cluster per region, not always
# the `-1` one — if yours differs (check with
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $LINODE_API_TOKEN" \
#     https://api.linode.com/v4/object-storage/endpoints
# ), pin it, e.g.: LINODE_STORAGE_REGION=us-iad-10
# Account-assigned cluster for us-iad (verified via GET /v4/object-storage/endpoints 2026-08-08)
LINODE_STORAGE_REGION=''

# ─── Vultr ── opt-in (`--provider vultr`, vultr/compose) ─────────────────────
# Not needed for the release-gating matrix. API key: 36 uppercase
# alphanumeric chars (my.vultr.com → Account → API; check Access Control —
# the API rejects calls from IPs outside the allowed subnets).
# VULTR_API_KEY is what @ediri/vultr reads; the token is set here.
VULTR_API_TOKEN=''

# Vultr Object Storage (S3-compatible) keys — created per Object Storage
# subscription in the Vultr console, separate credentials from the API token.
# (Archival tier @ ewr1, subscription 685bf9b1-897b-4b2e-b411-82e7e6e9fe19,
# created 2026-08-08.)
VULTR_ACCESS_KEY=''
VULTR_SECRET_KEY=''
VULTR_STORAGE_REGION=''

# ─── Scaleway ── opt-in (`--provider scaleway`, scaleway/compose) ────────────
# Not needed for the release-gating matrix. The credential is a TRIPLE, all
# three required together (the Pulumi provider demands the full set; the
# secret key alone drives the REST API as X-Auth-Token). The SAME pair
# signs Object Storage — there are no separate storage keys.
#
# ISOLATION (required): SCALEWAY_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID must name a DEDICATED
# Scaleway Project for e2e — SSH keys are Project-scoped and re-applied to
# EVERY instance in the Project at each boot, so a shared Project shares
# root access. Create the key at console.scaleway.com/iam/api-keys with an
# IAM APPLICATION as bearer (attach a policy first — an application has NO
# permissions until one is attached, and its key 401/403s every call), and
# answer the dialog's Object Storage question with "Yes, set up preferred
# Project" -> the SAME dedicated Project.
# EXPIRY: Scaleway keys expire (1-year org ceiling observed) and do so
# SILENTLY — set a renewal reminder or a future run 401s at deploy.
SCALEWAY_SECRET_KEY=''
SCALEWAY_ACCESS_KEY=''
SCALEWAY_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID=''

# ─── Docker Hub ── optional, all scenarios ───────────────────────────────────
# Authenticated image pulls raise the anonymous per-IP rate limit that
# restore/scale re-deploys can otherwise exhaust. A run without these falls
# back to anonymous pulls.
DOCKER_HUB_USERNAME=''
DOCKER_HUB_TOKEN=''
